WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:05.200
We're about to play a game
called "Box of Lies."

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.334
But I'm going to need some help.
Joining me is a very talented

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:11.133
actress who stars in the new
movie, "Scream VI,"

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:12.501
which is in theaters tomorrow.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:15.434
She's also hosting "Saturday
Night Live" this weekend

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:17.300
with musical guest, The 1975.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.801
Please welcome Jenna Ortega!

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:24.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.667
Alright. Now, Jenna, here's how
this works, okay?

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:31.067
We have nine mystery boxes
containing objects

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.701
no one has ever seen before.

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:34.367
On your turn, you pick a box,

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.767
take out the object,
describe it to your opponent.

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:37.834
Then they have to guess

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.767
if you're lying or telling
the truth.

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:43.334
Jenna, you pick the first box.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:46.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.701
[ Audience shouting numbers ]

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:49.934
-Three?

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:54.868
[ Drum roll ]

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.367
-You are choosing three.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.601
Huh, it looks --
it looks light.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:04.667
-[ Groans ]
-Yeah, too late.

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.601
Too late to act now.
-Now?

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:09.400
-Too late to act now.
I know it's light.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.300
Are you going to lie or are you
going to tell the truth?

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.100
Very interesting. Jenna Ortega.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:18.234
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:19.667
[ Tapping ]

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.467
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Interesting.
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.400
Oh, oh, I see.
You're making sounds.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.734
You're distracting me. Yeah.

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:26.901
-You don't know what's
happening to you.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.868
-What is in your box?

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.234
-Can I be honest with you,
Jimmy?

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:32.300
-Yes, you can always be honest
with me.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.033
-I don't -- I'm -- I'm not sure

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.300
I even understand
what's happening here.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:39.501
-You don't understand
what's happening?

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:42.868
So, this thing that you are now
looking at,

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:44.167
you don't understand.
-I don't.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.534
-Can you describe it?

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:47.167
-I fear of being a bit too
on the nose,

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:50.434
but it is
"Addams Family"-themed.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:51.567
-Yeah. Well, we knew that you
were coming on.

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:54.367
-Cousin Itt.
Yeah, well, it would make sense.

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:55.734
-It would make sense.
We did book you.

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:57.167
-Cousin Itt.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:02:01.167
He happens to be reading
a magazine of some sorts,

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:04.000
perhaps like "Vanity Fair"
Chewbacca edition?

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:07.400
-Cousin Itt is reading
a magazine

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.634
and it could be "Vanity Fair."
-Yeah, on a nice bench.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:13.601
-Bench? So, he's outside.
-Yeah, he's outside.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.334
It seems to be a nice park,
Central Park,

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.133
if you will, in New York.
-Oh, it's New York.

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:19.968
So he's in Central Park?
-There may be a corgi involved.

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:21.601
-It's a corgi?
-Yeah.

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:23.467
-So, Cousin Itt owns a dog?

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.901 --> 00:02:26.734
Cousin Itt owns a pet?

00:02:26.734 --> 00:02:29.167
-I guess so.
-So there's a lot of hair.

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:31.701
There's a lot of hair.
Is Cousin Itt wearing a hat?

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:34.334
-Yes, he is.
Like he always does.

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:36.567
He always has a hat.
-Yeah.

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.734
But if you took your time
answering that,

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.767
that would mean
that you're lying.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:43.834
So I think that you are...

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:46.133
telling the truth!

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:47.334
[ Drum roll ]

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:48.267
-I am.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:50.868
[ Ding! ]

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.334
-Wow!

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:53.467
"Vanity Fair."
-Honestly --

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:55.801
-Chewbacca? It's weird.
That is odd.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:58.701
-Yeah, I should have lied
because it's way too niche.

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:01.234
Like, the "Vanity Fair"
Chewbacca article, instantly --

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:02.534
-Yeah, we wouldn't do that.
Alright.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:04.300
[ Audience shouts numbers ]

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.734
[ Drum roll ]

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:08.133
-Two! Two!

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:13.734
-Oh, my back!

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:16.334
-I already did that.
-[ Groaning ]

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:20.934
Ooh!
-Ohh!

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.100
-Ooh! Here we go.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:26.767
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:30.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:37.601
It's a painting.

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:39.000
-Painting of what?

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.267
-Famous, famous,
famous painting.

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:42.801
Something you'd see in a museum.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:45.601
-I feel like you have to be
more specific on this game.

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.501
-I don't think -- I don't want
to be more specific.

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.801
I want to be vague.

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:52.234
Think of a famous painting.
-Oh, so it's just a painting.

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:55.000
Don't tell me it's
the Edvard Munch, the --

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.667
-"The Scream"?
-Ooh.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:58.501
-Ooh, that's interesting.
-That's a bit on the nose too.

00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:00.467
-Well, you do have a movie
called "Scream" coming out.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:02.501
So, that's pretty funny,
not niche.

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:03.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:09.133
Now, now, here's what makes it
funny.

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:14.133
It's not -- The painting's face.

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:15.767
It's Colonel Sanders.

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:19.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.033 --> 00:04:20.567
-Colonel Sanders is very funny.

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:22.400
-Colonel Sanders is funny.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.834
Kentucky Fried Chicken.

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:27.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.367
I love this.
In fact, I want to keep it

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:31.534
and hang it in my bedroom
because I love it.

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:33.234
It's so funny. There you go.

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.667
It's "The Scream,"
Colonel Sanders scream.

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:40.167
-Honestly, I feel like
Colonel Sanders is pretty funny.

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:42.734
Just to repeat myself.
-He's not supposed to be funny.

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:44.267
He's selling food.
-I think it's -- I think --

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:45.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.834 --> 00:04:47.300
♪♪

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:53.501
I feel like you might be telling
the truuuuu...

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:56.601
[ Woman shouts indistinctly ]

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.167
-Did you just say something
in Spanish?

00:04:58.167 --> 00:04:59.400
Wait, what did you just say?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.734
That's not fair.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.267
I feel like you just helped
somehow.

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:05.534
-Maybe it's a lie. Maybe it's a
lie. Maybe it's a lie.

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:07.033
Maybe two on-the-nose
references.

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:08.234
I'm sorry, I'm taking forever.

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:09.701
It's just 'cause
I really don't know.

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:11.434
I don't really care.
I'm going to go with truth.

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:14.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.467
-No! I was lying!
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:18.000
The "Mona Lisa."

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.701
-Oh, my God. You just took --
-Really a good actor.

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:21.968
Thank you.
-No.

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:24.000
-Did you say my acting skills
are fantastic?

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.367
That's so nice of you.
-Yeah, that's ex-- Yes.

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:29.334
-Thank you!

00:05:29.334 --> 00:05:30.868
Thank you!

00:05:30.868 --> 00:05:32.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.601
Time to pick a number.

00:05:33.601 --> 00:05:35.234
[ Audience shouts numbers ]
One more.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.400
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.467
-I'm serious.
-This is it.

00:05:39.467 --> 00:05:42.100
This is it.
For all the marbles.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:45.601
Jenna Ortega, pick a nombre.

00:05:48.534 --> 00:05:49.767
Uno.

00:05:49.767 --> 00:05:52.868
-Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Wow, it's a bowling ball.

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:55.400
It's a bowling ball. Wow.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:56.701
Alright, so it really is heavy.

00:05:56.701 --> 00:05:57.901
Oh, my goodness. Alright.

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.133
-What if I broke it
or something?

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:00.534
-Yeah.
-Okay. Sorry.

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:02.868
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:06:02.868 --> 00:06:11.834
♪♪

00:06:11.834 --> 00:06:14.834
-Why are you being --

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:16.734
Why are you being so serious?

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:20.734
♪♪

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:23.234
Roots, your music is, like,
giving me trips or something.

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:25.934
I'm tripping out.
I'm like, "Wah, wah."

00:06:27.601 --> 00:06:30.767
-Uh, we have, um...

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:32.200
It's a bobblehead.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.601
-What is it?

00:06:35.601 --> 00:06:37.367
-It's a bobblehead.
-It's a bobblehead?

00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:39.701
-A bobblehead of Peter Pan.

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:44.601
Um, he seems to be in a bit more
of a --

00:06:44.601 --> 00:06:48.234
like a -- like a business
attire.

00:06:48.234 --> 00:06:50.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.200
He's got kind of
like the Leonard Cohen --

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.133
-Peter Pan in, like,
a business suit?

00:06:53.133 --> 00:06:55.501
-Peter Pan in a business-esque
suit.

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:58.100
He's wearing a hat that's a bit
more of like

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.367
a Leonard Cohen fedora hat.

00:07:00.367 --> 00:07:01.767
And he's --
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.767 --> 00:07:03.968
-Leonard Cohen. That's so funny.

00:07:03.968 --> 00:07:07.200
-But it's also in a cowboy hat
with wheels

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.400
and marshmallows all in there.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:14.934
-Are you just naming words?
Are you just saying words?

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:15.901
-There are so many marshmallows
in there.

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:17.000
-You just said 20 words.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:17.868
-There's so many marshmallows
in there.

00:07:17.868 --> 00:07:19.434
-Peter Pan is on a marshmallow?

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:21.701
-No, there's -- So, cowboy hat.

00:07:21.701 --> 00:07:23.267
-Uh-huh.
-Truck wheels.

00:07:23.267 --> 00:07:25.701
-Yeah.
-Bunch of marshmallows in there.

00:07:25.701 --> 00:07:27.801
In there is a bobblehead
figurine of

00:07:27.801 --> 00:07:29.601
Peter Pan wearing
a business suit.

00:07:29.601 --> 00:07:31.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:32.667
-If you're lying,
it's pretty good.

00:07:32.667 --> 00:07:34.267
You have a good imagination.

00:07:35.834 --> 00:07:39.334
If you're telling the truth,
props to my props department.

00:07:39.334 --> 00:07:40.267
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.267 --> 00:07:41.901
Props to props.

00:07:41.901 --> 00:07:43.300
Welcome back to
"Props to Props."

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:44.834
-Yeah.

00:07:44.834 --> 00:07:47.801
-Jenna, I feel like
we're besties.

00:07:47.801 --> 00:07:49.367
And if we are, I would know

00:07:49.367 --> 00:07:50.801
if you're lying
or telling the truth.

00:07:50.801 --> 00:07:54.467
And I think you are...

00:07:54.467 --> 00:07:56.801
[ Drum roll ]

00:07:56.801 --> 00:08:00.734
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.734 --> 00:08:04.534
...telling ze truth!

00:08:04.534 --> 00:08:05.968
-I lie.
-Oh, my God!

00:08:05.968 --> 00:08:07.267
[ Buzzer ]

00:08:07.267 --> 00:08:08.434
[ Bell dinging ]

00:08:08.434 --> 00:08:10.367
Come on!

00:08:10.367 --> 00:08:12.234
Don't eat that. Don't eat that.

00:08:13.734 --> 00:08:16.100
Jenna Ortega, everybody!

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.567
Come right back.
More "Tonight Show."

00:08:17.567 --> 00:08:19.801
We're talking with Jenna.
Come on back, come on back.

